{"result": {"response": {"id": "chatcmpl-f1e91152-5b19-957e-b6f0-609a5d4ad3d7", "created": 1773048528, "model": "qwen-flash", "object": "chat.completion", "system_fingerprint": null, "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "{\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"explanation\": \"Chronic Migraine (CM) is a clinically significant condition affecting 1.4% to 2.2% of the general population and is associated with increased risks for psychiatric, psychological, respiratory, and cardiovascular diseases [Data: Entities (194), Relationships (292, 290)]. This condition represents a major health burden, as it is characterized by high headache frequency and can lead to substantial disability and reduced quality of life. The progression from episodic migraine to chronic migraine is a critical concern, particularly due to the risk of Medication Overuse Headache (MOH), which arises from frequent use of acute medications such as opioid analgesics on 10 or more days per month over three months [Data: Entities (155), Relationships (195)]. This transformation underscores the importance of preventive strategies in managing CM, as uncontrolled episodic migraine can evolve into a more debilitating chronic form. The condition's comorbidities further complicate treatment, requiring a multidisciplinary approach that considers both neurological and systemic health factors.\",\n            \"summary\": \"Chronic Migraine (CM) is a high-impact condition with significant health and disability implications\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"explanation\": \"A range of medications are used for the preventive treatment of Chronic Migraine (CM), including Type A Botulinum Toxin, Valproate, Propranolol, Metoprolol, Topiramate, and others [Data: Entities (194, 197, 196, 198, 568, 567), Relationships (290, 292, 803, 808, 813, 818, 837)]. These drugs are selected based on efficacy, safety profiles, and patient-specific factors such as comorbidities and ph